From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cryolitia PukNgae <cryolitia@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 02:32:50 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] PCI: qcom: sequence controller and PHY clocks before reset

Keep the Piano-specific parts of the xiaomi-piano-nixos PCIe reset
sequence after importing the original Qualcomm patches. Enable endpoint
power before initializing the PHY, route CLKREQ# before PHY start and
configure the remaining PARF registers with the PHY running. Preserve
CSR programming when possible and stop the data path on power-off.
Unwind only ports that acquired resources.

This adaptation also carries forward slwyts's related PCIe bring-up
changes from the SunUEFI platform port. The independently usable SID
and suspend changes from that port are kept as separate commits.

The upstream no-CSR reset regression fix is applied before the
HPG PHY split. The board sequencing and retained-CSR handling here
build on that reset policy.

Link: https://github.com/Cryolitia/xiaomi-piano-nixos/commit/b06301d14f50ee09e995aae50ecbaac05e89f55e
Link: https://github.com/slwyts/Project-SunUEFI/commit/e8fcf33971263f28085dbc0dbe5039438bf76c13
---
 drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-qcom.c   | 217 +++++++++++++++++------
 drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-pcie.c | 131 +++++++-------
 2 files changed, 227 insertions(+), 121 deletions(-)

